  "articleBody": "It's awesome to tackle home projects yourself, but sometimes a kitchen addition needs a professional touch. How do you know when it's time to call in the experts? Well, if your project involves changing the structure of your home, adding square footage, or messing with things like drainage, electrics, or ventilation, you're definitely in pro territory. These types of changes almost always require permits and building regulations approval, and you'll need someone who knows how to navigate that. Also, if you're dealing with a listed building, you might need special Listed Building Consent, which can be tricky. Even if your project falls under permitted development rules, getting building control sign-off is usually a must. A qualified builder or extension specialist, like HH Remodeling LLC in Aurora, Colorado, can coordinate all those moving parts for you. They’ll ensure everything is done correctly, safely, and up to code, saving you potential headaches down the line. Don't risk costly mistakes or safety issues; when in doubt, get a professional opinion.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}